  "post_hoc_disclosure": "docs/RESEARCH_QUESTIONS.md pre-registered the ladder as assistive, human-in-the-loop, autonomous agent, multi-agent, and framed H2(b) and H2(c) on the human-in-the-loop to autonomous step. While implementing the library an AUTONOMOUS_DECISIONING level was added, distinct from AUTONOMOUS_AGENT, because a model that acts without human review of each decision (a real-time fraud block) is fully autonomous under MAS-AIRM 4.12(c) but has no tools, so the agent attributes of 4.8 fn25 do not apply to it. That change moved the step the hypotheses named. H2(b) and H2(c) are reported as refuted on their original wording. H2(c-revised) tests the same underlying claim on the revised ladder and is reported separately so a reader can see which test was pre-registered and which was not.",
